Although Soledad works in a windowless office, she loves the outdoors. She will be on vacation for the entire month of June and cannot wait to hike 9,300 miles within that month. She is thinking of walking twice a day, covering 125 miles each time. How many more miles per day must Soledad hike to complete her journey on time?
Soledad wants to hike 9,300 miles in a month. There are 30 days in a month. To figure out how many miles she needs to hike per day, we can do 9,300 / 30 = 310. So she would need to hike 310 miles per day. However, she is thinking of walking twice a day, covering 125 miles each time. This would be 2 x 125 = 250 miles per day. So she would need to hike 310 - 250 = 60 more miles per day. The answer is 60.
